cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Recrystal: A Layout Parser for Research Papers"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Choudhary
    given-names: Mudit
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-8880-0925"
repository-code: "https://github.com/mudit-choudhary/recrystal"
url: "https://github.com/mudit-choudhary/recrystal"
abstract: >-
  Parses research-paper PDFs into ordered, typed blocks: a YOLO11 layout
  detector fine-tuned on 12 research-paper classes finds the regions, PyMuPDF
  supplies the words, and textreflow rebuilds reading order and paragraphs.
  In a pre-registered evaluation over 514 papers and 400 questions it lost 24
  answer spans in parsing against Docling's 48 and PyMuPDF4LLM's 61, and
  parsed 2.88x faster per page than Docling on a 4 GB consumer GPU.
keywords:
  - document parsing
  - layout analysis
  - research papers
  - retrieval-augmented generation
license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
version: 1.0.0
